{"raw": {"https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/louisiana/northwesternstate/jobs/5169349/adjunct-instructor-welding-technology": {"title": "ADJUNCT INSTRUCTOR-WELDING TECHNOLOGY", "description": "ADJUNCT INSTRUCTOR-WELDING TECHNOLOGY Salary See Position Description Location Natchitoches, LA Job Type Unclassified Job Number FA0008 Department Northwestern State University Opening Date 12/12/2025 Description Benefits About this Job The Department of Engineering Technology at Northwestern State University of Louisiana invites applications for an Adjunct Instructor to teach a course in Welding Technology during the Spring 2026 semester. The successful candidate will deliver both theoretical instruction and hands-on laboratory guidance to undergraduate students pursuing careers in Associate of Science in Engineering Technology with Advanced Manufacturing Concentration. The course focuses on \"An introduction to the principles of shielded metal arc welding and cutting with a plasma torch and oxyfuels. Safe handling and use of the welding equipment, consumables, and safety gears. Basic hands-on practices on various types of welding joints using arc welding cutting mild steel with Plasma torch and Oxyfuel.\" The instructor will be responsible for classroom instruction, lab supervision, assessment of student learning outcomes, and maintaining a safe and effective learning environment. Application Review: Begins immediately and continues until the position is filled. Appointment: Spring Semester 2027 (January-May) Schedule: Tuesday & Thursday, 11:00 AM-1:05 PM Compensation: $2,000 per semester (may differ depending on qualification) Contract: Semester-based appointment; renewable annually based on departmental needs, performance, and funding availability. To Apply: Submit \u2022Cover letter describing qualifications and teaching interests \u2022Curriculum vitae or resume \u2022Copies of relevant certifications \u2022Contact information for two professional references Send to: Dr. Md Shahriar Hossain, Department Head & Associate Professor Department of Engineering Technology, Northwestern State University of Louisiana, Natchitoches, LA Williamson Hall, Room IOI, Natchitoches, LA 71497, Phone: 318-357-5026, Email: hossains@nsula.edu NOTICE OF NON-DISCRIMINATION (FULL DISCLOSURE) Northwestern State University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws. This policy applies to all terms and conditions of employment, including recruiting, hiring, placement, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, transfer, leaves of absence, compensation and training. All complaints or inquiries related to Title IX should be directed to the Director of Title IX Compliance and Title IX Coordinator, Julie Powell (318-357-5570), Room 306 of the Friedman Student Union or email obannonj@nsula.edu . In accordance with Section 35.106 of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), all participants, applicants, organizations, and interested individuals are advised and notified that the ADA Coordinator for Northwestern State University for facilities is the Director of University Affairs, Jennifer Kelly (318-357-4300), located in New Fine Arts, 104 Central Avenue, Ste. 102 or email andersonje@nsula.edu . For student academic services , contact the Director of Access and Disability Support, Crissey Smith (318-357-5460) located in Room 108-C Watson Memorial Library or email smithcr@nsula.edu . For faculty/staff accommodations and services , contact Executive Director of Institutional Effectiveness and Human Resources, Veronica M. Biscoe (318-357-6359), Room 111 Caspari Hall or email ramirezv@nsula.edu . Minimum Qualifications Associate degree in Welding Technology or closely related field; (Equivalent technical certificate + industry experience considered.) 3-5 years of professional welding experience (fabrication, construction, inspection, or related industry experience). Current welding certifications (A WS or equivalent) in applicable welding processes. Demonstrated proficiency in multiple welding processes ( e.g., SMAW, GMA W, GTA W, FCAW). Ability to interpret welding blueprints, symbols, specifications, and applicable welding codes. Strong communication skills and a demonstrated ability to teach and mentor students. Meets state requirements for vocational/technical instructor eligibility at the postsecondary level. Job Duties and Other Information \u2022Teach the assigned Welding Technology course on Tuesdays and Thursdays, 11:00 AM-1:0SPM. \u2022Provide instruction in welding theory and hands-on welding applications. \u2022Demonstrate safe use of tools, equipment, and welding processes. \u2022Evaluate student performance through assignments, lab work, and examinations. \u2022Maintain accurate records of attendance and grades in accordance with NSU policies. \u2022Ensure adherence to shop safety procedures and OSHA regulations. \u2022Prepare instructional materials, including syllabi, lesson plans. and assessments. \u2022Support department goals and ABET-related student outcomes as applicable. \u2022Perform other duties related to effective instruction as assigned by the Department Head. Benefits for unclassified employees are determined by the individual hiring authority. Employer State of Louisiana Address 1201 N 3rd St Baton Rouge, Louisiana, 70802 Phone (866) 783-5462 Website http://agency.governmentjobs.com/louisiana/default.cfm"}, "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/louisiana/northwesternstate/jobs/4742163/assistant-associate-professor-of-biology": {"title": "ASSISTANT/ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR OF BIOLOGY", "description": "ASSISTANT/ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR OF BIOLOGY Salary $60,000.00 - $65,000.00 Annually Location Natchitoches, LA Job Type Unclassified Job Number 999449 Department Northwestern State University Opening Date 08/27/2026 Description Benefits About this Job The Louisiana Scholars' College, the state's selective-admission honors college of the liberal arts and sciences, located at Northwestern State University of Louisiana, seeks applications from broadly trained individuals to fill a tenure-track position as an Assistant/ Associate Professor of Biology with an anticipated start date of either January 4, 2027 or August 9, 2027, depending on the successful candidate\u2019s availability . Review of applications will begin immediately. To Apply: Interested qualified candidates should send, by email, cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, all college transcripts, representative publications or a dissertation chapter, and contact information for three professional references to the address listed below. Women, minorities, and individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Official transcripts must be received prior to any offer of employment. Assistant/ Associate Professor of Biology Search Committee Louisiana Scholars' College Northwestern State University Natchitoches, LA 71497 scholars@nsula.edu Northwestern State University is a State as a Model Employer (SAME) agency. The successful candidate will be subject to a background check, as a condition of employment. Notice of Non-Discrimination (Full Disclosure) Northwestern State University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws. This policy applies to all terms and conditions of employment, including recruiting, hiring, placement, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, transfer, leaves of absence, compensation, and training. All complaints or inquiries related to Title IX should be directed to the Director of Title IX Compliance and Title IX Coordinator, Julie Powell (318-357-5570), Room 306 of the Friedman Student Union or email tix@nsula.edu. In accordance with Section 35.106 of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), all participants, applicants, organizations, and interested individuals are advised and noticed that the ADA Coordinator for Northwestern State University for facilities is the Director of University Affairs, Jennifer Kelly (318-357-4300), located in Room 128 Caspari Hall or email andersonje@nsula.edu. For student academic services, contact the Director of Accessibility and Disability Support, Crissey Smith (318-357-5460) located in Room 111 Watson Memorial Library or email smithcr@nsula.edu. For faculty/staff accommodations and services, contact Executive Director of Institutional Effectiveness and Human Resources, Veronica M. Biscoe (318-357-6359), Room 111 Caspari Hall or email ramirezv@nsula.edu. Minimum Qualifications Qualifications The successful candidate must have an earned Ph.D. in Biology or a related field. The successful candidate will be able to teach introductory and advanced undergraduate honors biology courses, as well as be able and willing to contribute to a team-taught Core/Great Texts curriculum. Preference will be given to applicants with prior college-level teaching experience, experience directing student research, and experience in honors education. The successful candidate will have demonstrated evidence of scholarly achievement. Applicants should be committed to liberal arts education and willing to interact with colleagues and students from other fields in the arts and sciences to maintain and improve an integrated, multidisciplinary honors curriculum. Job Specification Job Concepts Duties include teaching 12-15 contact hours per semester; holding 1O office hours per week; advising students as assigned; directing undergraduate theses as needed; maintaining a research agenda; developing curricula; and working on committees as assigned. Benefits for unclassified employees are determined by the individual hiring authority. Employer State of Louisiana Address 1201 N 3rd St Baton Rouge, Louisiana, 70802 Phone (866) 783-5462 Website http://agency.governmentjobs.com/louisiana/default.cfm"}, "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/louisiana/northwesternstate/jobs/5379861/assistant-associate-professor-of-nursing": {"title": "ASSISTANT/ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR OF NURSING", "description": "ASSISTANT/ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR OF NURSING Salary $74,000.00 - $78,000.00 Annually Location Shreveport, LA Job Type Unclassified Job Number 999061 Department Northwestern State University Opening Date 06/16/2026 Description Benefits About this Job Northwestern State University College of Nursing and School of Allied Health seeks an applicant for a 12-month full-time faculty position for the Associate/Bachelor of Science degree programs in nursing available in Shreveport, or off-campus instructional site. Academic rank and salary commensurate with qualifications and experience. Review of applications will begin immediately. Position will remain open until filled. To Apply: Submit 1) a letter of application, 2) an updated CV, 3) official transcripts (if not from NSU) and 4) a list of three professional references with complete contact information to: Tamara Baxter, Department Head and Interim Senior Director, College of Nursing, Northwestern State University, 175 Sam Sibley Drive, Natchitoches, LA 71497 or email baxtert@nsula.edu . Mailed documents are preferred. Notice of Non-Discrimination (Full Disclosure) Northwestern State University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws. This policy applies to all terms and conditions of employment, including recruiting, hiring, placement, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, transfer, leaves of absence, compensation, and training. All complaints or inquiries related to Title IX should be directed to the Director of Title IX Compliance and Title IX Coordinator, Julie Powell (318-357-5570), Room 306 of the Friedman Student Union or email tix@nsula.edu. In accordance with Section 35.106 of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), all participants, applicants, organizations, and interested individuals are advised and noticed that the ADA Coordinator for Northwestern State University for facilities is the Director of University Affairs, Jennifer Kelly (318-357-4300), located in Room 128 Caspari Hall or email andersonje@nsula.edu. For student academic services, contact the Director of Access and Disability Support, Crissey Smith (318-357-5460) located in Room 111 Watson Memorial Library or email smithcr@nsula.edu. For faculty/staff accommodations and services, contact Executive Director of Institutional Effectiveness and Human Resources, Veronica M. Biscoe (318-357-6359), Room 111 Caspari Hall or email ramirezv@nsula.edu. Minimum Qualifications A Masters in Nursing required, however, a Doctorate is preferred (required for academic rank of Associate Professor); Eligible for membership on undergraduate and graduate faculty. Unencumbered licensure status as an RN or APRN in the state of Louisiana; or eligible for Louisiana licensure. At least three (3) years of clinical nursing experience. At least three (3) years of nurse educator experience; three (3) or more preferred. Must be able to pass a background check and shall meet the required standards defined by the University. Job Duties and Other Information Duties and Responsibilities: \u2022Preform faculty responsibilities in a large, nursing education department at Northwestern State University located on the Shreveport Campus. \u2022Assist with program expansion in Natchitoches and surrounding areas. \u2022Teach all classes in a manner that will fully promote academic excellence. \u2022Provide instruction in areas of expertise. \u2022Evaluate student learning experiences. \u2022Serve as a role model to students and peers. \u2022Reflect on the university in a positive manner. \u2022Assist with maintenance of records and files pertinent to the College of Nursing. \u2022Maintain confidentiality regarding faculty and students in accordance with federal laws and program and university policies. \u2022Assist with the development, evaluation and revision of policies and procedures within the College of Nursing. \u2022Attend College of Nursing and/or university functions and committee meetings as assigned. \u2022Maintain required regular office hours and excellent attendance. \u2022Advise and counsel students during office hours and/or at other times and settings as needed. \u2022Participate in activities that promote the College of Nursing, including those that may occur in the evenings, out of town and/or on the weekend. \u2022Be flexible, collaborative, and cooperative about all college and university activities, maintaining a positive, respectful, and supportive attitude. \u2022Recruit students to all programs within the College of Nursing and School of Allied Health. \u2022Serve as a Liaison between the College of Nursing and other university departments as well as local, state, and national agencies and professional organizations. \u2022Comply with university, state, SACSCOC, ACEN, CCNE and/or other guidelines as required. \u2022Serve on department or college-wide committees and/or state level committees/boards on behalf of NSU CON. \u2022Represent the college and university positively in interactions with professional and academic groups at local, state, and national levels. \u2022Utilize a variety of proven teaching methods appropriate to student population and targeted domain of learning. \u2022Participate in periodic review of course materials, including development of course reports. \u2022Maintain appropriate expertise and competencies through continuing professional development and pursuit of scholarly activities including teaching pedagogy, grant writing, research, scholarly publication, and presentations. \u2022Demonstrate knowledge of and adherence to College of Nursing's goals, values, and objectives. MOTOR, STRENGTH, AND MOBILITY SKILLS \u2022Manipulate equipment (locks, push buttons, knobs, switches, and medication administration equipment) using fine motor skills. \u2022Complete delicate procedures in a timely and accurate manner. \u2022Safely push a wheelchair, stretcher, or other transport equipment from a patient waiting area or patient room to other parts of the facility. \u2022Safely transfer a patient from a wheelchair or stretcher to the bed or exam table. \u2022Raise arms above head and in all directions to manipulate equipment. \u2022Stand and walk for extended periods of time (up to 12 hours). \u2022Lift twenty-five (25) pounds of weight and at minimum, ten (10) pounds above head. \u2022Perform all aspects of CPR, ACLS, PALs, and Basic Life Support as required by specific clinical program. \u2022Employ diagnostic reasoning (select graduate students). COMMUNICATION SKILLS \u2022Communicate effectively in English (via verbal and written means) with patients, family members, physicians, and all members of the health care team. \u2022Read and quickly comprehend written instructions to deliver appropriate patient care. \u2022Document written and electronic records and assignments in an accurate and timely manner. \u2022Willingly receive and provide feedback. \u2022Process and communicate information on the patient's status with accuracy, in a timely manner, to members of the healthcare team. SENSORY (HEARING, VISION, TACTILE AND OLFACTORY) SKILLS \u2022Hear sufficiently to interact with patients and medical staff when background noise is present. \u2022Detect audible sounds within the hospital, such as equipment alarms, fire alarms, telephones ringing, and overhead pages. Benefits for unclassified employees are determined by the individual hiring authority. Employer State of Louisiana Address 1201 N 3rd St Baton Rouge, Louisiana, 70802 Phone (866) 783-5462 Website http://agency.governmentjobs.com/louisiana/default.cfm"}, "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/louisiana/northwesternstate/jobs/5260013/assistant-associate-professor-of-veterinary-technology": {"title": "ASSISTANT/ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR OF VETERINARY TECHNOLOGY", "description": "ASSISTANT/ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR OF VETERINARY TECHNOLOGY Salary $76,000.00 - $80,000.00 Annually Location Natchitoches, LA Job Type Unclassified Job Number 999185 Department Northwestern State University Opening Date 03/05/2026 Description Benefits About this Job The Department of Veterinary Technology at Northwestern State University of Louisiana seeks applications from enthusiastic individuals interested in a tenure-track Assistant/ Associate Professor of Veterinary Technology starting August 10, 2026 . Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. To Apply: Interested candidates should email their curriculum vitae (CV) or resume, a statement of teaching philosophy, unofficial copies of graduate transcripts, and the names and contact information for three professional references to : Kaleigh MacQueen, Department Head. Email: macqueenk@nsula.edu . *NOTE: Official copies of transcripts and proof of a Louisiana license is due at time of hire. NOTICE OF NON-DISCRIMINATION (FULL DISCLOSURE) Northwestern State University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws. This policy applies to all terms and conditions of employment, including recruiting, hiring, placement, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, transfer, leaves of absence, compensation and training. All complaints or inquiries related to Title IX should be directed to the Director of Title IX Compliance and Title IX Coordinator, Julie Powell (318-357-5570), Room 306 of the Friedman Student Union or email obannonj@nsula.edu . In accordance with Section 35.106 of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), all participants, applicants, organizations, and interested individuals are advised and notified that the ADA Coordinator for Northwestern State University for facilities is the Director of University Affairs, Jennifer Kelly (318-357-4300), located in New Fine Arts, 104 Central Avenue, Ste. 102 or email andersonje@nsula.edu . For student academic services , contact the Director of Access and Disability Support, Crissey Smith (318-357-5460) located in Room 108-C Watson Memorial Library or email smithcr@nsula.edu . For faculty/staff accommodations and services , contact Executive Director of Institutional Effectiveness and Human Resources, Veronica M. Biscoe (318-357-6359), Room 111 Caspari Hall or email ramirezv@nsula.edu . Minimum Qualifications \u2022Doctor of Veterinary Medicine (DVM) from an AVMA accredited program \u2022 Must hold a current license in the state of Louisiana \u2022Ability to teach a combination of undergraduate lecture and laboratory courses within a Veterinary Technology program. \u2022Demonstrated knowledge in one or more of the following areas: General Veterinary Technology, Veterinary Medical Terminology, Pharmacology, Anatomy and Physiology, Animal Care and Health, Diseases of Animals, Clinical Parasitology, Hospital Technology, Veterinary Radiology Job Duties and Other Information \u2022Teach assigned undergraduate lecture and laboratory courses in the Veterinary Technology curriculum. \u2022Evaluate students regularly and reports progress in a timely manner. \u2022Participate in program assessment, curriculum review, and continuous improvement efforts. \u2022Participates in faculty meetings and serves on all appropriate department and university committees. \u2022Maintains confidentiality in accordance with federal laws and university policy. \u2022Assist with AVMA-CVTEA accreditation activities, including documentation, data collection, and preparation for site visits and reports. \u2022Maintain clinical relevance through professional development or clinical practice. \u2022Contribute to departmental, program, and university service activities. \u2022Support student advising, mentoring, recruitment, and retention efforts. \u2022Represents the Department in a professional manner in all activities. \u2022Committed to excellence in teaching, service, and professional growth. \u2022Willingness to contribute to recruitment and retention initiatives. Benefits for unclassified employees are determined by the individual hiring authority. Employer State of Louisiana Address 1201 N 3rd St Baton Rouge, Louisiana, 70802 Phone (866) 783-5462 Website http://agency.governmentjobs.com/louisiana/default.cfm"}, "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/louisiana/northwesternstate/jobs/5380455/assistant-associate-professor-msn-pmc-faculty": {"title": "ASSISTANT/ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR-MSN/PMC FACULTY", "description": "ASSISTANT/ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR-MSN/PMC FACULTY Salary $60,000.00 - $65,000.00 Annually Location Alexandria, LA Job Type Unclassified Job Number 999196 Department Northwestern State University Opening Date 06/17/2026 Description Benefits About this Job Northwestern State University College of Nursing and School of Allied Health seeks an applicant for a 9-month full-time faculty position in the MSN/PMC Program available in Alexandria, LA beginning August 10, 2026. Academic rank commensurate with qualifications and experience. Review of applications will begin immediately. Only complete applications will be reviewed. Position will remain open until filled. To Apply: Submit Curriculum Vitae along with three (3) professional reference to: Dr. Aaron Stigers, MSN & PMC Programs Director, College of Nursing, Northwestern State University, 1800 Line Avenue, Shreveport, LA 71101-3127 or stigersa@nsula.edu Fax# 318-677-3127. Notice of Non-Discrimination (Full Disclosure) Northwestern State University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws. This policy applies to all terms and conditions of employment, including recruiting, hiring, placement, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, transfer, leaves of absence, compensation, and training. All complaints or inquiries related to Title IX should be directed to the Director of Title IX Compliance and Title IX Coordinator, Julie Powell (318-357-5570), Room 306 of the Friedman Student Union or email tix@nsula.edu. In accordance with Section 35.106 of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), all participants, applicants, organizations, and interested individuals are advised and noticed that the ADA Coordinator for Northwestern State University for facilities is the Director of University Affairs, Jennifer Kelly (318-357-4300), located in Room 128 Caspari Hall or email andersonje@nsula.edu. For student academic services, contact the Director of Access and Disability Support, Crissey Smith (318-357-5460) located in Room 111 Watson Memorial Library or email smithcr@nsula.edu. For faculty/staff accommodations and services, contact Executive Director of Institutional Effectiveness and Human Resources, Veronica M. Biscoe (318-357-6359), Room 111 Caspari Hall or email ramirezv@nsula.edu. Minimum Qualifications Master of Science in Nursing required; Doctorate preferred. National certification as a Family Nurse Practitioner required. Louisiana license as Advanced Practice Registered Nurse, and a minimum of three years clinical nurse practitioner experience required. At least three (3) years of nurse educator experience; three (3) or more preferred. Must be able to pass a background check and shall meet the required standards defined by the University. Job Duties and Other Information Recruit's students to all programs within the College of Nursing. Serves as Liaison between the College of Nursing and clinical affiliation sites. Complies with university, state, ACEN, CCNE and NONPF guidelines. Maintains 10 on-campus office hours. Advises and counsels students during required hours and at other times and settings as established by the Dean, Department Head, or Director. Maintains Clinical practice as an advanced practice nurse. Maintains certification from National Certification Agency (AANP or ANCC) for respective specialties. Teaches in MSN/PMC courses and other courses as established by Dean, Department Head or Director. Provide instruction in areas of expertise. Teach undergraduate (if assigned) and graduate nursing courses in a manner that promotes academic excellence to the fullest extent. Evaluate students and report their progress. Utilize a variety of teaching strategies appropriate to domain of learning. Serve as a role model to students and peers. Assist with development, evaluation and revision of curriculum, and policies and procedures within the College of Nursing. Maintain required 10 on-campus office hours. Supervise and evaluate student learning experiences. Teach across programs as needed Participate in student clinical learning/practice with affiliated agencies. Serve as an advisor and mentor for students in the College of Nursing. Recruit students to all programs within the College of Nursing and School of Allied Health. Advise students interested in the program and those currently in the program regarding the curriculum and APDG requirements. Attend College of Nursing, University functions, and committee meetings as assigned. Maintain records and files related to undergraduate and graduate nursing courses. Maintain weekly office hours and advise students during required office hours or at other times and settings established by the Dean, Senior Director of Nursing, or Program Director. Demonstrate knowledge of the College of Nursing goals and objectives. Assist with maintenance of records and files pertinent to the College of Nursing. Maintain confidentiality in accordance with federal laws and program policy. Serve as a Liaison between the College of Nursing and other University departments as well as local, state, and national agencies and professional organizations as assigned. Comply with guidelines/regulations of the University, state of Louisiana, SACSCOC, LSBN, CCNE, NONPF and/or other agencies as required.Actively participate in scholarly activities and other creative activities, such as, scholarly research; writing books, book chapters, and/or articles; practice; podium or poster presentations; etc. Maintain appropriate expertise and competencies through continuing professional education, and development and pursuit of scholarly activities. Serve on college-wide committees and state level committees and boards on behalf of the NSU CON when selected by the Dean or designee. Volunteer as a nurse practitioner provider at a local clinic for the underserved community. Maintain practice as an Advanced Practice Registered Nurse in your field of specialty Serve as an advisor and mentor for students in the College of Nursing Represent the College of Nursing and University in a professional manner. Participate in activities that promote the College of Nursing, including those that may occur in the evenings, out of town and on the weekend. Assist the concentration coordinator with assigned tasks and program improvement. Review program curriculum and courses as a Program Curriculum Committee (PCC) member to ensure program is congruent with national certification and accreditation standards. Oversee clinical learning for assigned students to ensure consistency with the population focused knowledge and that the sites and preceptors provide opportunities for students to learn and perform necessary skills. Attend and contribute to student program orientation at the beginning of each semester. Ensure clinical preceptors hold current, unencumbered professional licensure and other requirements for a clinical preceptorship as set forth by the program, National Task Force (NTF), and CCNE accreditation guidelines. Support clinical students and address/escalate any student issues or needs as they arise. Communicate with students after graduation for pertinent survey data. Maintain a positive attitude. Demonstrate flexibility and knowledge of the College of Nursing's goals and objectives. Collaborate outside of the specialty concentration to improve the student learning experience throughout the CONSAH. Perform any other duties as assigned by the Program Director, Senior Director, Dean, or University Administration. Benefits for unclassified employees are determined by the individual hiring authority. Employer State of Louisiana Address 1201 N 3rd St Baton Rouge, Louisiana, 70802 Phone (866) 783-5462 Website http://agency.governmentjobs.com/louisiana/default.cfm"}, "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/louisiana/northwesternstate/jobs/4971905/doctor-of-nursing-practice-program-director-assistant-associate-professor-nursing": {"title": "DOCTOR OF NURSING PRACTICE PROGRAM DIRECTOR ASSISTANT/ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR-NURSING", "description": "DOCTOR OF NURSING PRACTICE PROGRAM DIRECTOR ASSISTANT/ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR-NURSING Salary $90,000.00 - $95,000.00 Annually Location Shreveport, LA Job Type Unclassified Job Number 999612 Department Northwestern State University Opening Date 06/12/2025 Description Benefits About this Job Northwestern State University College of Nursing and School of Allied Health seeks a Doctor of Nursing Practice Director in Shreveport or Off-Campus Instructional site in Louisiana. The review of applications will begin immediately, and the position will remain open until filled. Only complete applications will be reviewed. To Apply: Submit 1} a letter of application, 2) an updated CV, 3) official transcripts (if not from NSU}, 4) a list of three professional references with complete contact information to: Dr. Anna Morris Department Head and Senior Director, College of Nursing Northwestern State University 1800 Line Avenue Shreveport, LA, 71101-3127 morrisa@nsula.edu NOTICE OF NON-DISCRIMINATION (FULL DISCLOSURE) Northwestern State University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws. This policy applies to all terms and conditions of employment, including recruiting, hiring, placement, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, transfer, leaves of absence, compensation and training. All complaints or inquiries related to Title IX should be directed to the Director of Title IX Compliance and Title IX Coordinator, Julie Powell (318-357-5570), Room 306 of the Friedman Student Union or email obannonj@nsula.edu . In accordance with Section 35.106 of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), all participants, applicants, organizations, and interested individuals are advised and notified that the ADA Coordinator for Northwestern State University for facilities is the Director of University Affairs, Jennifer Kelly (318-357-4300), located in New Fine Arts, 104 Central Avenue, Ste. 102 or email andersonje@nsula.edu . For student academic services , contact the Director of Access and Disability Support, Crissey Smith (318-357-5460) located in Room 108-C Watson Memorial Library or email smithcr@nsula.edu . For faculty/staff accommodations and services , contact Executive Director of Institutional Effectiveness and Human Resources, Veronica M. Biscoe (318-357-6359), Room 111 Caspari Hall or email ramirezv@nsula.edu . Minimum Qualifications MINIMAL QUALIFICATIONS: Applicants must be nursing research or nursing practice doctorate prepared and hold an unencumbered Louisiana license as a registered nurse. Applicants must also have significant administrative/leadership experience in higher education and in developing and/or coordinating DNP curricula/programs. Must have experience in building practice education partnerships and demonstrate strong interpersonal/oral written communication skills. Teaching experience at the doctoral nursing level is preferred. Applicants must show evidence of ongoing scholarly activity, adeptness at online educational technology, and be eligible to serve as a full member of Northwestern State University's Graduate Faculty. The doctoral studies director will report directly to the College of Nursing's Senior Director of Nursing and indirectly to the College of Nursing's Dean. Job Specification \u2022Be responsible for all aspects of the DNP program, including, but not limited to supervising and evaluating program faculty/staff, leading continuous quality improvement efforts, maintaining accreditation requirements, and developing/updating curricula and or new concentrations. \u2022Exploring and leading appropriate workforce-need-driven program expansion efforts that will add to the imminence of the college and university. \u2022Creating vibrant, inclusive, creative, rigorous, active-learning experiences for all students who choose NSU's DNP program. \u2022Ensuring sufficient numbers of qualified doctoral faculty to lead quality programs. \u2022Creating a passionate, respectful, transparent workplace environment for all program faculty and staff. \u2022Be committed to excellence in teaching, service, professional growth, scholarship and professional service. \u2022Maintaining required office hours and excellent attendance, while teaching online and face to face course in doctoral nursing \u2022Representing the College of Nursing and the University in a professional manner and role modeling professional behaviors expected of all DNP faculty. \u2022Supervising and evaluates student learning experiences. \u2022Creatively recruiting students for all concentrations within the DNP Program. \u2022Performing any other duties as assigned by the Senior Director, Dean, or University Administration. Job Duties and Other Information Reports to: Senior Director for the College of Nursing and Dean of the College of Nursing and School of Allied Health Duties and responsibilities: Serves as faculty and administrator responsible for the Doctor of Nursing Practice Programs in the College of Nursing. Description (% Effort): 12-month tenure-track appointment Administrative Duties (30%) \u2022Responsible for all aspects of the DNP program, including, but not limited to supervising faculty, leading continuous quality improvement efforts, maintaining accreditation requirements, and developing/updating curricula and or new concentrations. \u2022Serves as a liaison between the College of Nursing and other University departments as well as local, state, and national agencies and professional organizations. \u2022Ensures program is compliant with guidelines/regulations of the University, regional accreditation (SACSCOC) standards, national accreditation (GOA and CCNE) standards, and state regulatory agencies (LSBN), and/or other agencies as required. \u2022Explores and leads appropriate workforce-need-driven program expansion efforts that will add to the imminence of the college and university. \u2022Provides visionary leadership to shape the strategic direction of the DNP program, ensuring alignment with the College of Nursing's vision, mission, goals, and strategic plan. \u2022Ensures program tuition/fees/budgetary decisions are made in a timely manner that is beneficial to all stakeholders. \u2022Creates vibrant, inclusive, creative, rigorous, active-learning experiences for all students who choose NSU's DNP program. \u2022Works with the Senior Director of Nursing and the CONSAH Dean to develop program support funding. \u2022Collaborates with nursing faculty to review and revise curricula and programs to ensure that offerings are relevant, rigorous, and meet the needs of the healthcare community. \u2022Ensures sufficient numbers of qualified doctoral faculty to lead quality programs. \u2022Evaluates all program faculty and staff in accordance with NSU's faculty evaluation policies and established faculty outcomes. \u2022Role-models the professional behaviors expected of all DNP faculty. \u2022Creates semester schedules and directing faculty workload assignments that are equitable and in accord with the College of Nursing's workload policy. \u2022Creates a passionate, respectful, transparent workplace environment for all program faculty and staff. \u2022Leads concentration coordinators in program development, recruitment, and retention activities \u2022Encourages and supports scholarship and innovation in program faculty. Teaching Duties (20%): \u2022Teaches an equitable didactic and/or clinical class load in accordance with the College of Nursing's workload policy. \u2022Maintains expertise in areas of teaching responsibility. \u2022Utilizes a variety of teaching strategies appropriate to the domain of learning. \u2022Maintains required office hours and attendance. \u2022Supervises and evaluates student learning experiences. Scholarly Activities and Professional Development (20%): \u2022Actively participates in University and college of nursing committees, including acting as chair of the DNP Program Curriculum Committee (DN P PCC) \u2022Actively participates in scholarly activities and other creative activities, such as, scholarly research; writing books, book chapters, and/or articles; practice; podium or poster presentations. \u2022Maintains appropriate expertise and competencies through continuing professional education and development, as well as through the pursuit of scholarly activities. \u2022Participates in relevant state and national professional development activities to stay abreast of requirements and up-to-date knowledge required from DNP graduates. Student Engagement: Advising and Recruiting (15%): \u2022Creatively recruits students for all concentrations within the DNP Program. \u2022Ensures the program provides quality advising and instruction in online, distance, and face-to-face settings. \u2022Advises applicants interested in the DNP program and advises currently enrolled students. \u2022Works with the alumni office to develop a doctorate graduate alumni base. Service (10%): \u2022Attends College of Nursing and/or University functions and committee meetings as assigned. \u2022Representing the CON to internal and external stakeholders at college, university, state, regional and national events. \u2022Represents the College of Nursing and University in a professional manner. \u2022Participates in activities that promote the College of Nursing, including those that may occur in the evenings, out of town and on the weekend. Other (5%): Responsible for maintenance of records and files pertinent to the College of Nursing. \u2022Maintains confidentiality in accordance with federal laws and program policy. \u2022Performs any other duties as assigned by the Senior Director, Dean, or University Administration. Benefits for unclassified employees are determined by the individual hiring authority. Employer State of Louisiana Address 1201 N 3rd St Baton Rouge, Louisiana, 70802 Phone (866) 783-5462 Website http://agency.governmentjobs.com/louisiana/default.cfm"}, "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/louisiana/northwesternstate/jobs/5518535/assistant-professor-of-nursing": {"title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OF NURSING", "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OF NURSING Salary $74,000.00 - $76,000.00 Annually Location Alexandria, LA Job Type Unclassified Job Number 998933 Department Northwestern State University Opening Date 10/15/2026 Description Benefits About this Job Northwestern State University College of Nursing and School of Allied Health seeks an applicant for a 12-month full-time faculty position for the Associate/Bachelor of Science degree programs in nursing available in Alexandria/Cenla or off-campus instructional site. Anticipated start date: Upon completion of the hiring and approval process. Academic rank and salary commensurate with qualifications and experience. Review of applications will begin immediately. Position will remain open until filled. To Apply: Submit 1) a letter of application, 2) an updated Cl/, 3) official transcripts (if not from NSU) and 4) a list of three professional references with complete contact information to: Dr. Melissa Rennie, Shreveport Campus Director, College of Nursing, Northwestern State University, 1800 Line Avenue, Shreveport, LA, 71101 or coxm@nsula.edu . Notice of Non-Discrimination (Full Disclosure) Northwestern State University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws. This policy applies to all terms and conditions of employment, including recruiting, hiring, placement, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, transfer, leaves of absence, compensation, and training. All complaints or inquiries related to Title IX should be directed to the Director of Title IX Compliance and Title IX Coordinator, Julie Powell (318-357-5570), Room 306 of the Friedman Student Union or email tix@nsula.edu. In accordance with Section 35.106 of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), all participants, applicants, organizations, and interested individuals are advised and noticed that the ADA Coordinator for Northwestern State University for facilities is the Director of University Affairs, Jennifer Kelly (318-357-4300), located in Room 128 Caspari Hall or email andersonje@nsula.edu. For student academic services, contact the Director of Accessibility and Disability Support, Crissey Smith (318-357-5460) located in Room 111 Watson Memorial Library or email smithcr@nsula.edu. For faculty/staff accommodations and services, contact Executive Director of Institutional Effectiveness and Human Resources, Veronica M. Biscoe (318-357-6359), Room 111 Caspari Hall or email ramirezv@nsula.edu. Minimum Qualifications \u2022Master's degree in Nursing required; Doctorate preferred. \u2022Eligibility for membership in the undergraduate faculty. \u2022Unencumbered RN license in the state of Louisiana, or eligibility for licensure. \u2022Minimum of three (3) years of clinical nursing experience. \u2022Minimum of three (3) years of nurse educator experience; more than three years preferred. \u2022Demonstrated ability to build positive relationships with students and colleagues. \u2022Proficiency (or ability to become proficient) in curriculum development, instruction, student evaluation, and academic advising. \u2022Ability to pass a criminal background check. \u2022Must meet all university-defined standards for academic appointment. Job Duties and Other Information \u2022 Teach all classes in a manner that fully promotes academic excellence. \u2022 Provide instruction in areas of expertise. \u2022 Evaluate student learning experiences. \u2022 Serve as a role model to students and peers. \u2022 Represent the university in a positive manner. \u2022 Assist with the maintenance of records and files pertinent to the College of Nursing. \u2022 Maintain confidentiality regarding faculty and students in accordance with federal laws and program and university policies. \u2022 Assist with the development, evaluation, and revision of policies and procedures within the College of Nursing. \u2022 Attend College of Nursing and/or university functions and committee meetings as assigned. \u2022 Maintain required regular office hours and excellent attendance. \u2022 Advise and counsel students during office hours and/or at other times and in other settings as needed. \u2022 Participate in activities that promote the College of Nursing, including those that may occur in the evenings, out of town, and/or on weekends. \u2022 Be flexible, collaborative, and cooperative in all college and university activities while maintaining a positive, respectful, and supportive attitude. \u2022 Recruit students to all programs within the College of Nursing and School of Allied Health. \u2022 Serve as a liaison between the College of Nursing and other university departments, as well as local, state, and national agencies and professional organizations. \u2022 Comply with university, state, SACSCOC, ACEN, CCNE, and/or other guidelines as required. \u2022 Serve on departmental or college-wide committees and/or state-level committees or boards on behalf of the NSU College of Nursing. \u2022 Represent the college and university positively in interactions with professional and academic groups at local, state, and national levels. \u2022 Utilize a variety of proven teaching methods appropriate to the student population and targeted domain of learning. \u2022 Participate in periodic reviews of course materials, including the development of course reports. \u2022 Maintain appropriate expertise and competencies through continuing professional development and the pursuit of scholarly activities, including teaching pedagogy, grant writing, research, scholarly publication, and presentations. \u2022 Demonstrate knowledge of and adherence to the College of Nursing\u2019s goals, values, and objectives. Benefits for unclassified employees are determined by the individual hiring authority. Employer State of Louisiana Address 1201 N 3rd St Baton Rouge, Louisiana, 70802 Phone (866) 783-5462 Website http://agency.governmentjobs.com/louisiana/default.cfm"}, "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/louisiana/northwesternstate/jobs/5519418/assistant-professor-of-political-science-economics-or-philosophy": {"title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OF POLITICAL SCIENCE, ECONOMICS, OR PHILOSOPHY", "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OF POLITICAL SCIENCE, ECONOMICS, OR PHILOSOPHY Salary $60,000.00 - $65,000.00 Annually Location Natchitoches, LA Job Type Unclassified Job Number 999448 Department Northwestern State University Opening Date 10/16/2026 Description Benefits About this Job The Louisiana Scholars' College, the state's selective-admission honors college of the liberal arts and sciences, located at Northwestern State University of Louisiana, seeks applications to fill two tenure-track positions as an Assistant Professor of Economics, Political Science, or Philosophy with an anticipated start date of August 9, 2027. One of these positions will be filled by an applicant with at least 18 credit hours of graduate coursework in economics; otherwise, the specializations for these positions are open. Review of applications will begin on October 1, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. The successful candidates must have an earned Ph.D. in Economics, Political Science, or Philosophy. The successful candidates will be able to teach introductory and advanced undergraduate honors courses in their fields, as well as be able and willing to contribute to a team-taught core Great Texts curriculum. Preference will be given to applicants with prior college-level teaching experience, experience directing student research, and experience in honors education. Duties include teaching 12-15 contact hours per semester; holding 10 office hours per week; advising students as assigned; directing undergraduate theses as needed; maintaining a research agenda; developing curricula; and working on committees as assigned. To Apply: Interested, qualified candidates should send, by email (with \"Assistant Professor of PPE\" in the subject line), to scholars(a), nsula.edu : Cover letter, Curriculum Vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, representative publication (no more than 30 pages), contact information for three professional references, and all college transcripts (unofficial are acceptable for the preliminary application, official may be requested at a later date). Women, minorities, and individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Assistant Professor of PPE, Search Committee Louisiana Scholars' College Northwestern State University Natchitoches, LA 71497 scholars@nsula.edu Notice of Non-Discrimination (Full Disclosure) Northwestern State University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws. This policy applies to all terms and conditions of employment, including recruiting, hiring, placement, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, transfer, leaves of absence, compensation, and training. All complaints or inquiries related to Title IX should be directed to the Director of Title IX Compliance and Title IX Coordinator, Julie Powell (318-357-5570), Room 306 of the Friedman Student Union or email tix@nsula.edu. In accordance with Section 35.106 of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), all participants, applicants, organizations, and interested individuals are advised and noticed that the ADA Coordinator for Northwestern State University for facilities is the Director of University Affairs, Jennifer Kelly (318-357-4300), located in Room 128 Caspari Hall or email andersonje@nsula.edu. For student academic services, contact the Director of Accessibility and Disability Support, Crissey Smith (318-357-5460) located in Room 111 Watson Memorial Library or email smithcr@nsula.edu. For faculty/staff accommodations and services, contact Executive Director of Institutional Effectiveness and Human Resources, Veronica M. Biscoe (318-357-6359), Room 111 Caspari Hall or email ramirezv@nsula.edu. Minimum Qualifications \u2022Shall be qualified to teach in field of study \u2022Shall be effective in teaching the assigned subject material \u2022Shall meet the required standards defined by the University \u2022Shall be proficient in curriculum development, instruction, assessment, and academic advising \u2022Shall hold a doctoral degree in History or a related field Job Duties and Other Information \u2022Be committed to excellence in teaching, service, and professional growth and scholarship \u2022Teach all courses in a manner that promotes academic excellence \u2022Submit course outlines and objectives \u2022Utilize a variety of proven teaching methods appropriate to pedagogy \u2022Evaluate students and report progress \u2022Participate in periodic review of course materials \u2022Maintain assigned class schedules and the required 10 hours of office hours per week as determined by the Director \u2022Demonstrate knowledge of the goals and objectives of the program, College, and University \u2022Serve as an advisor and mentor for students in the Louisiana Scholars' College \u2022Direct undergraduate research and serve as a reader on honors theses \u2022Participate in faculty meetings and serve on all appropriate program, College, and University committees \u2022Maintain appropriate expertise and competencies through continued professional development and pursuit of scholarly activities, including grant writing, research, scholarly publication, and presentations \u2022Represent the University in a professional manner in all activities and functions as determined by the President, Vice President for Academic Affairs, Dean, or Director (e.g., commencement, faculty institute, registration, and all called meetings) \u2022Maintain confidentiality in accordance with federal laws and program, College, and University policies \u2022Acknowledge and agree to comply with those mandates of the Constitution and laws of the State of Louisiana which regulate the activity and employment of state employees including but not limited to the \"Code of Government Ethics,\" \"LA R.S. 42: 1101 et seq.,\" and \"Dual Office Holding and Dual Employment LA R.S. 42:61 et seq.\" Benefits for unclassified employees are determined by the individual hiring authority. Employer State of Louisiana Address 1201 N 3rd St Baton Rouge, Louisiana, 70802 Phone (866) 783-5462 Website http://agency.governmentjobs.com/louisiana/default.cfm"}, "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/louisiana/northwesternstate/jobs/5519442/associate-director-of-bands-and-assistant-professor-of-music": {"title": "ASSOCIATE DIRECTOR OF BANDS AND ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OF MUSIC", "description": "ASSOCIATE DIRECTOR OF BANDS AND ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OF MUSIC Salary $73,000.00 Annually Location Natchitoches, LA Job Type Unclassified Job Number 999540 Department Northwestern State University Opening Date 10/16/2026 Description Benefits About this Job Northwestern State University is currently seeking qualified applicants for the position of Associate Director of Bands and Assistant Professor. This is a 12-month position at the rank of Assistant Professor tenure-track position and is commensurate with experience and qualifications. Anticipated start date of July 1, 2027. Review of applications begins immediately. To Apply: Review of applications will begin immediately. Deadline: December 1, 2026 Please send the following materials via email in one PDF file: application letter, vita, transcripts (unofficial at this time), names and contact information for five references, links to a marching band and/or concert band rehearsal (and performance if possible), and other appropriate credentials to: Mr. Scott Burrell, Director The Dear School of Creative and Performing Arts Northwestern State University Natchitoches, LA 71497 Email: capa@nsula.edu Notice of Non-Discrimination (Full Disclosure) Northwestern State University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws. This policy applies to all terms and conditions of employment, including recruiting, hiring, placement, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, transfer, leaves of absence, compensation, and training. All complaints or inquiries related to Title IX should be directed to the Director of Title IX Compliance and Title IX Coordinator, Julie Powell (318-357-5570), Room 306 of the Friedman Student Union or email tix@nsula.edu. In accordance with Section 35.106 of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), all participants, applicants, organizations, and interested individuals are advised and noticed that the ADA Coordinator for Northwestern State University for facilities is the Director of University Affairs, Jennifer Kelly (318-357-4300), located in Room 128 Caspari Hall or email andersonje@nsula.edu. For student academic services, contact the Director of Accessibility and Disability Support, Crissey Smith (318-357-5460) located in Room 111 Watson Memorial Library or email smithcr@nsula.edu. For faculty/staff accommodations and services, contact Executive Director of Institutional Effectiveness and Human Resources, Veronica M. Biscoe (318-357-6359), Room 111 Caspari Hall or email ramirezv@nsula.edu. Minimum Qualifications 1.Minimum degree-Masters required; doctorate preferred; 2.Evidence of successful teaching experie??ce at high school and/or the college level with marching bands and concert bands. Job Duties and Other Information Duties and Responsibilities Teaching Direct all aspects of the Spirit of Northwestern Marching Band. Oversee faculty and student leadership of the Purple Haze Basketball Pep Band. Conduct the Fall Winds concert ensemble (fall semester) and the Wind Ensemble (spring semester). Teach courses based on the candidate\u2019s qualifications and departmental needs, including undergraduate conducting and a student leadership and development course. Improving Teaching, Assessment, etc. Teach online, in-person, and hybrid courses. Demonstrate knowledge of program goals and objectives. Submit course outlines and objectives. Maintain class schedules. Provide course instruction in accordance with the developed syllabus. Advise/mentor students. Utilize a variety of proven teaching methods appropriate to targeted domains of learning. Evaluate students and report progress. Participate in periodic review of course materials. Scholarship Maintain appropriate expertise and competencies through continuing professional development and pursuit of scholarly activities. Participate in scholarly activities, including grant writing, research, scholarly publication, and presentations. Service: Band Program Administration/Activities Assist the Director of Bands in fostering an environment and culture that inspires students to grow and supports the educational focus and institutional objectives of the band program and university by attending and participating in all marching band-related events. Actively recruit prospective students through a variety of activities and initiatives on and off campus; actively engage with outreach efforts to public school band programs throughout the region. Coordinate and lead efforts for successful athletic band recruiting events, including Young Performers Day and Classic on the Cane Marching Festival. Assist with band area scholarship auditions, contracts, renewals, etc. Work with the Director of Bands to coordinate performances, tours, and programming for all related band activities. Serve as faculty advisor/co-advisor to either Kappa Kappa Psi (KKY) or Tau Beta Sigma (TBS) band service organizations. Maintain and update the athletic band program\u2019s presence and information on the departmental website. Assist the Director of Bands in the upkeep and oversight of program inventories, including athletic band instruments and marching uniforms. Coordinate and supervise students and staff for the annual Summer Music Camps. Attend and collaborate in band staff meetings and maintain open and collaborative communication with colleagues. Attend campus-wide meetings representing the band staff as requested by the Director of Bands. Service: Departmental/University/Profession Actively participate and represent NSU, CAPA, the Department of Music, and the band program at state, regional, and national conventions as needed. Establish and maintain positive relationships with stakeholders, the instrumental faculty, ensemble directors, and other departments/programs across campus. Participate in departmental faculty meetings and serve on all appropriate programs and committees in the Dear School of Creative and Performing Arts and Department of Music. Serve as a Graduate Faculty Member and chair/serve as a committee member of graduate student committees and guide graduate research as requested. Maintain confidentiality in accordance with federal laws and policy. Engage in professional service. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the Director of Bands, Department Chair, or CAPA Director from assigning additional duties that logically relate to the position. Benefits for unclassified employees are determined by the individual hiring authority. Employer State of Louisiana Address 1201 N 3rd St Baton Rouge, Louisiana, 70802 Phone (866) 783-5462 Website http://agency.governmentjobs.com/louisiana/default.cfm"}}, "rows": {"https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/louisiana/northwesternstate/jobs/5169349/adjunct-instructor-welding-technology": {"school_id": 517, "posting_url": "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/louisiana/northwesternstate/jobs/5169349/adjunct-instructor-welding-technology", "job_title_in_post": "ADJUNCT INSTRUCTOR-WELDING TECHNOLOGY", "position_type": "Associate_Professor", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "Department of Engineering Technology", "area_key_words": "Welding Technology", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/louisiana/northwesternstate/jobs/4742163/assistant-associate-professor-of-biology": {"school_id": 517, "posting_url": "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/louisiana/northwesternstate/jobs/4742163/assistant-associate-professor-of-biology", "job_title_in_post": "ASSISTANT/ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR OF BIOLOGY", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor; Associate_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "college of the liberal arts and sciences, located", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": "January 4, 2027"}, "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/louisiana/northwesternstate/jobs/5379861/assistant-associate-professor-of-nursing": {"school_id": 517, "posting_url": "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/louisiana/northwesternstate/jobs/5379861/assistant-associate-professor-of-nursing", "job_title_in_post": "ASSISTANT/ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR OF NURSING", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor; Associate_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "College of Nursing", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/louisiana/northwesternstate/jobs/5260013/assistant-associate-professor-of-veterinary-technology": {"school_id": 517, "posting_url": "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/louisiana/northwesternstate/jobs/5260013/assistant-associate-professor-of-veterinary-technology", "job_title_in_post": "ASSISTANT/ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR OF VETERINARY TECHNOLOGY", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor; Associate_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "Department of Veterinary Technology", "area_key_words": "Veterinary Technology curriculum", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/louisiana/northwesternstate/jobs/5380455/assistant-associate-professor-msn-pmc-faculty": {"school_id": 517, "posting_url": "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/louisiana/northwesternstate/jobs/5380455/assistant-associate-professor-msn-pmc-faculty", "job_title_in_post": "ASSISTANT/ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR-MSN/PMC FACULTY", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor; Associate_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "College of Nursing", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/louisiana/northwesternstate/jobs/4971905/doctor-of-nursing-practice-program-director-assistant-associate-professor-nursing": {"school_id": 517, "posting_url": "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/louisiana/northwesternstate/jobs/4971905/doctor-of-nursing-practice-program-director-assistant-associate-professor-nursing", "job_title_in_post": "DOCTOR OF NURSING PRACTICE PROGRAM DIRECTOR ASSISTANT/ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR-NURSING", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor; Associate_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "College of Nursing's Dean", "area_key_words": "nursing \u2022Representing the College of", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/louisiana/northwesternstate/jobs/5518535/assistant-professor-of-nursing": {"school_id": 517, "posting_url": "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/louisiana/northwesternstate/jobs/5518535/assistant-professor-of-nursing", "job_title_in_post": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OF NURSING", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "College of Nursing", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/louisiana/northwesternstate/jobs/5519418/assistant-professor-of-political-science-economics-or-philosophy": {"school_id": 517, "posting_url": "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/louisiana/northwesternstate/jobs/5519418/assistant-professor-of-political-science-economics-or-philosophy", "job_title_in_post": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OF POLITICAL SCIENCE, ECONOMICS, OR PHILOSOPHY", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "college of the liberal arts and sciences, located", "area_key_words": "OR PHILOSOPHY; willing", "deadline_of_application": "October 1, 2026", "position_start_date": "August 9, 2027"}, "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/louisiana/northwesternstate/jobs/5519442/associate-director-of-bands-and-assistant-professor-of-music": {"school_id": 517, "posting_url": "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/louisiana/northwesternstate/jobs/5519442/associate-director-of-bands-and-assistant-professor-of-music", "job_title_in_post": "ASSOCIATE DIRECTOR OF BANDS AND ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OF MUSIC", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "Department of Music, and the band program", "area_key_words": "Direct all aspects of the", "deadline_of_application": "December 1, 2026", "position_start_date": "July 1, 2027"}}, "school_id": 517, "status": "complete", "updated_at": "2026-10-16T18:44:02+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-10-16T18:44:02+00:00", "last_error": ""}